From: Cheng Wang <chengwa@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kimi-k3): disable cuDNN for MoonViT Conv2d patch-embed on GB200 (nvbug 6608287)

On GB200 TP=16 with VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=0, cudnnCreate() called
concurrently across 16 mp-executor processes sharing the MNNVL symmetric-
memory region triggers a native segfault inside MoonVision3dPatchEmbed._proj.
Disabling cuDNN for that single Conv2d forces the non-cuDNN fallback kernel
and avoids the crash. GB300 with VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1 is unaffected.

--- a/vllm/model_executor/models/kimi_k25_vit.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/models/kimi_k25_vit.py
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
     def _proj(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
         if current_platform.is_rocm() and x.dtype in (torch.float16, torch.bfloat16):
             from aiter.ops.triton.conv.conv2d import conv2d
             return conv2d(x, self.proj.weight, self.proj.bias, stride=self.patch_size, layout="nchw")
-        return self.proj(x)
+        with torch.backends.cudnn.flags(enabled=False):
+            return self.proj(x)
